## Component (Unit)
Tests one function/class in isolation. Manual QA rarely does this — developers do.
Example: A "calculateDiscount()" function returns 10% for Gold members.

## Integration
Tests data flow between components. **Manual QA lives here.**
Example: Postman sends POST /users → DBeaver confirms the row exists in the users table.

## System
Tests the whole app end-to-end against requirements.
Example: Complete checkout on an e-commerce site: add to cart → pay → confirm order email.

## Acceptance
Tests business/user needs. Often UAT.
Example: A finance user confirms an invoice can be generated and exported to PDF.

**Where I spend most time as manual QA:** Integration + System.
